# The argument of `L2:` is taken as it is written (the book #two-kinds-of-receivers: the arguments of L2 are not opened as code): one written
# Structure after the colon is the ONE field of the record, and a Structure among the statements of a code body runs nothing -- the same as a
# Structure written as a line of a sub body. The two records inside it do not run: `seen` and `after` stay 0 and the dump shows one Structure under L2.
# наблюдение явной записью: локалы не публикуются (#flush-receiver-contract)
(
    Observed:
        int: seen 0
        int: after 0
)
@: shared data[0]
L2: (shared\Observed\seen := 5; shared\Observed\after := 6)
